Foundation post-WP-05 verification update

Stage 5 WP-05 full final validation completed successfully on governed technical baseline `fbf9b1a4c7b89efd44c3ea092ae689dac3894168`.

For FCR-0005, the WP-05-owned generic producer-to-consumer routing/isolation portion is now verified satisfied:
- producer/Application and intended-consumer binding;
- admitted message/message-type binding;
- recipient-scope consistency;
- declared route eligibility;
- route/endpoint isolation;
- deterministic fail-closed rejection and routing evidence;
- no market-data-specific Foundation route.

WP-05 does NOT satisfy actual delivery, duplicate-effect handling, degradation signaling, acknowledgements, retries, queueing, backpressure, flow control, or delivery-outcome semantics.

`FCR_0005_WP05_PORTION = VERIFIED_SATISFIED`
`FCR_0005_OVERALL = REMAINS_OPEN_FOR_DELIVERY_SEMANTICS`
`FCR_CLOSURE = NOT_YET_ELIGIBLE`

Foundation evidence: `docs/stage-5-wp05/06_FINAL_VALIDATION_AND_EVIDENCE_RECONCILIATION.md`, `07_INDEPENDENT_POST_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.md`, and `08_FCR_AND_COMPLETENESS_RECONCILIATION.md`.

Stage 5 WP-06 pre-validation reconciliation update

Foundation performed a fresh WP-06-specific review of FCR-0005 before runtime validation.

WP-06-owned generic portions confirmed in scope:
- producer-to-consumer delivery attempt semantics after accepted admission/routing;
- bounded retry and explicit terminal containment;
- duplicate-effect protection through idempotency-aware retry policy;
- destination-health and bounded failure/degradation handling;
- flow control/backpressure decisions;
- truthful transport outcome evidence.

Foundation will not implement market-data-specific quality/business semantics inside MessageDelivery. Schema/version compatibility remains predecessor-owned; business quality/confidence interpretation remains Application-owned.

`FCR_0005_WP06_RELEVANCE = DIRECT_PARTIAL`
`FCR_0005_WP06_STATUS = IMPLEMENTATION_IN_PROGRESS`
`MARKET_DATA_SPECIAL_CASE = PROHIBITED`
`FCR_0005_OVERALL = REMAINS_OPEN_PENDING_IMPLEMENTATION_VALIDATION_AND_APPLICATION_VERIFICATION`

Foundation evidence: `docs/stage-5-wp06/05_FCR_PRE_VALIDATION_DISPOSITION.md` and `06_FCR_PRE_VALIDATION_STATUS_SNAPSHOT.md`.

WP-06 focused-validation update on `foundation-development`.

Validated technical HEAD: `90112de5dc7f8b04b83f6b1b6b233e4bb92e93e2`.

WP-06-owned FCR-0005 portions now focused-runtime-verified:
- generic producer/consumer transport delivery semantics after accepted routing;
- accepted expiry/freshness boundary preservation;
- idempotency-aware retry/duplicate-effect protection;
- bounded destination-health / degradation handling;
- governed pressure gating and isolation;
- immutable delivery attempt/outcome evidence.

Evidence: `docs/stage-5-wp06/09_FOCUSED_VALIDATION_EVIDENCE.md`; WP-06 verifier `58/58 PASS` twice.

Remaining outside or after WP-06 focused validation:
- market-data quality/confidence business semantics remain Application-owned;
- event/replay truth remains later-owned;
- Application-side verification;
- full final Foundation regression / independent closure-readiness review;
- final FCR reconciliation before any closure decision.

`FCR_OVERALL = REMAINS_OPEN`.
